USFthesis -- LaTeX thesis and dissertation template
University of South Florida
Bellini College of Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Computing

Adapted by Nima Karimian from SJSUthesis.cls (David C. Anastasiu, San Jose
State University), which is itself derived from IEEEtran.cls V1.8b (Michael
Shell). This is a MODIFIED version, renamed per the LaTeX Project Public
License; it is not the original SJSU class and is not endorsed by its
original authors.

Distributed under the LPPL v1.3, as-is and without warranty.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUILDING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

  pdflatex main
  bibtex mainbib          <-- note: mainbib, NOT main
  pdflatex main
  pdflatex main

The class writes citations to a separate auxiliary file (mainbib.aux), so
bibtex is run on "mainbib" rather than on "main". latexmk will not figure
this out on its own.

Sample figures referenced by sections.tex live in a figures/ subdirectory
that is not included here; missing-file errors from those \includegraphics
calls are harmless and disappear once you add your own figures.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

  USFthesis.cls       The class file. You should not need to edit this.
  IEEEtran.cls        Required base class.
  main.tex            Preamble and front-matter metadata. Start here.
  sections.tex        Body chapters.
  abstract.tex        Abstract (required).
  dedication.tex      Dedication (optional).
  acknowledgments.tex Acknowledgments (optional).
  abbreviations.tex   List of abbreviations (optional).
  appendices.tex      Appendices (optional).
  aboutauthor.tex     About the Author page (USF requirement; optional in
                      the class, enable it in main.tex).
  references.bib      BibTeX database.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
FRONT-MATTER MACROS (set these in main.tex)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

  \title{...}            Manuscript title.
  \author{...}           Must match the name on file with Graduate Studies.
  \copyrightholder{...}  Name on the copyright line.
  \copyrightyear{...}    Defaults to the current year.
  \university{...}       Defaults to University of South Florida.
  \college{...}          Defaults to Bellini College of Artificial
                         Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Computing.
  \department{...}       Department name (also aliased as \dept).
  \degreename{...}       Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Science, etc.
  \concentration{...}    Optional; leave empty to omit the line entirely.
  \committee{Name}{Dept} Once per member; the first is the Major Professor.
  \approvaldate{...}     Last date signed by the committee.
  \keywords{...}         Five terms, comma separated, none already in the
                         title.
  \aboutauthor{file}     Enables the About the Author page.

IMPORTANT: the degree macro is \degreename, not \degree. The gensymb
package loaded by main.tex already defines \degree, and the collision is a
fatal error.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLASS OPTIONS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

  dissertation | thesis | project         Default: dissertation
  3committee | 4committee | 5committee    Default: 4committee
  9pt | 10pt | 11pt | 12pt                Default: 12pt
  copyrightpage | nocopyrightpage         Default: nocopyrightpage
  tables, figures                         List of tables / figures pages
  draft | final                           Default: final

Example:  \documentclass[dissertation,5committee]{USFthesis}


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED FROM THE SJSU ORIGINAL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Title page rebuilt to the USF format: title, "by", author, the degree
   statement, concentration, department, college, university, committee
   list, Date of Approval, Keywords, and the copyright line at the foot.

2. The SJSU Library Rights Statement page was removed. USF handles
   distribution rights through the ETD submission agreement.

3. The typeset committee approval page was removed. USF files a separately
   signed Certificate of Approval with the Graduate School; the committee
   appears on the title page instead. \committeepage is retained as a no-op
   so older documents still compile.

4. The standalone copyright page is now opt-in (copyrightpage option),
   since USF puts the copyright line on the title page.

5. Added an About the Author page after the appendices.

6. Front-matter order changed to USF's: title, dedication, acknowledgments,
   abstract, table of contents, list of tables, list of figures.

7. New metadata macros (see above) and a new "dissertation" class option.

8. BUG FIX, not cosmetic: the upstream class set the TOC, LOF, and LOT
   headings with \MakeUppercase\contentsname, \MakeUppercase\listfigurename,
   and \MakeUppercase\listtablename. Under current LaTeX releases, applying
   \MakeUppercase to those IEEEtran-defined names sends the compiler into an
   infinite loop -- the build stalls silently just after the abstract page
   with no error message. The headings are now written out literally. If you
   copy any other heading from the upstream class, do not reintroduce that
   pattern.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
BEFORE YOU SUBMIT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

This template encodes the USF format as of the sources consulted when it
was built. Formatting requirements change. Download the current USF
Graduate Studies / College of Engineering ETD format guide and check your
manuscript against it -- particularly margins, page-number placement, and
the exact wording of the title page -- before submitting for format review.
